✅ 8. What is an Interface?
A contract that defines what methods/properties
 a class must implement.
No implementation inside interface.

✅ What is a Constructor in C#?
A constructor is a special method in a class that is automatically called when an object is created.
It is used to initialize the object with default or custom values.

✅ 6. OOPs Concepts

Encapsulation: Wrapping data and methods into a single unit (class) and restricting direct access using access modifiers.
Inheritance: One class (child) inherits the properties and methods of another (parent), allowing code reuse.
Polymorphism: Same method behaves differently (overload/override).
🔹 Method Overloading :Same method name with different parameter types or counts.
🔹 Method Overriding : Child class provides a new implementation of a virtual method from the parent class.
Abstraction: Hiding complex logic and showing only essentials using abstract classes or interfaces.

✅ 9. What is Dependency Injection?
A design pattern that allows injecting dependencies
(services) into a class, rather than creating them inside the class.
Promotes loose coupling.

 ✅ DI Lifetimes and Registration in Program.cs ?

 | Lifetime  | Description                            |
| --------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Singleton | One instance for the app lifetime      |
| Scoped    | One instance per HTTP request          |
| Transient | New instance every time it's requested |

✅ 12. What is LINQ (Language Integrated Query)?
A way to query collections or databases using C# syntax.

✅ What is a Delegate in C#?
A delegate is a type-safe function pointer — it allows you to store
 references to methods and call them dynamically at runtime.
Delegates are often used for callbacks, event handling, and passing methods as parameters.

✅ 2. How .NET Works ?
CLR (Common Language Runtime): Executes the code.
BCL (Base Class Library): Provides core functionality.
Compilation process:
Source code → IL (Intermediate Language)
IL → JIT compiled to native code during execution


✅ What is the role of the CLR (Common Language Runtime)?
CLR is the execution engine for .NET apps.
It handles JIT compilation, memory management, garbage 
collection, type safety, and exception handling.


✅ 19. What is Entity Framework Core?
An ORM for .NET Core.
Allows interacting with databases using C# objects.

✅ How Do You Handle Global Exceptions in ASP.NET Core?
n ASP.NET Core, global exception handling ensures all 
unhandled exceptions are caught in one place — usually
 via middleware — so you don’t need try-catch in every controller


✅ 3. What is Middleware in ASP.NET Core?

Middleware are components in the HTTP pipeline that 
handle requests/responses.
Examples: Authentication, Logging, CORS, Static Files.

